  "body": "The 1812 fort's parade slab already draws through the native fenced-ground layer. The building loader still required a direct building batch for it, producing a false missing-building error and potentially suppressing dependent furniture. This accounts separately for the two explicitly owned parade grounds only after their real loaded meshes prove finite, nonempty and entirely earth with valid triangles. Direct building counts and boxes remain actual geometry. Failed loads, malformed or empty meshes, mixed earth/sundial geometry and unknown owners retain ordinary presence checks.\n\nActual validation:\n\n- Local source parts 1\u20133 passed on unchanged authored tree `44ce86cc`; whole part 4 passed on `fa943206` after the native instrument genuinely measured the new read-only regression. The original isolation-coverage failure remains preserved. Fresh current-dev owner checks and production parade, 54 fort-gate, batch-coalescing and batch-instancing regressions passed.\n- Frozen head `05366ebe` passed actual 1812 cards plus a positive native parade-ground GPU hit at both desktop and phone, then existing published 1835 Stage 3 at both sizes: **107 passed, 0 failed each**. All four legs and the whole controller properly reaped every child; all 720 selected inputs, 5887 published members and Git/helper guards remained exact. Both custom legs had zero page/network/console/server errors.\n- Root directly reviewed all eight card JPGs. Full Quaife Record and Currey link-only Images credit are visible at both sizes; the full Whistler citation is visible on desktop. The phone source screenshot shows Quaife/Swearingen, with Whistler item 6 off screen; the long roof reason is clipped, at both ends on phone. No complete phone Whistler, whole-long-reason, roof-body or full fort image-match claim.\n- Later Lake documentary metadata and the independently reviewed Cobweb aperture increment are normally integrated. Renderer fix, first-fort 1812 data/physical assets, and NE/parade manifest contracts remain unchanged. The Lake audit proves its geometry/function/confidence/yard items unchanged. **The actual 1835 native runs used the older pre-Cobweb scene**, not the current one; scoped carry composes unchanged owned contracts with the coordinator-approved [fixed Cobweb comparison](https://github.com/kevinrhaas/chicago-evidence/blob/57a69573a54e56f3b25880f7718ff343ea25cd86/evidence/cobweb-castle-2026-11-04/ee8529e-fixed-private-depth-pair/RECOVERY.md). No current whole-scene byte-equivalence or new browser execution is claimed. Fresh current owners/staleness, aperture/parade/fort regressions and metadata checks pass; final required hosted eight-part gate is pending.\n\nThis continues existing T-3041 / parent T-2387 and does not close their original image gates. Visible-progress exemption: it removes the actual scene-validation error blocking the owner-adopted north-east pyramid-roof parcel from PR #1685. The ground already rendered. No new photo ticket or restored-ground claim.\n\n[Closed actual runtime and native receipts](https://github.com/kevinrhaas/chicago-evidence/blob/d2d1a4203849bc597338d6a08a1cbd7da0727a6d/evidence/first-fort-2026-11-04/pr1696-runtime-closed-pass/RECOVERY.md) \u00b7 [Eight JPGs and bounded direct review](https://github.com/kevinrhaas/chicago-evidence/blob/f73332e4c9f02ffcea1edb4c0e4343a279448c9f/evidence/first-fort-2026-11-04/pr1696-both-cards-positive-ground-root-reviewed/RECOVERY.md)\n",
